  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>With rise in temperature, Young’s modulus of  elasticity decreases due to the increase in atomic <br/>vibrations which leads to decrease in atomic forces. The Young's modulus is a measure of stiffness of the material. With rise in temperature, the length of the material increases which decreases its stiffness.</p>",
